Third-party material
====================

The native jars carry libraries of the official llama.cpp release builds, unchanged, from the release archives named in
gradle.properties. Each native jar carries the licence texts of its libraries in org/fogofwarlabs/llama/<platform>/licenses/,
and every jar carries LICENSE and this NOTICE in META-INF/. The classes of org.fogofwarlabs.llama.bindings are generated by
jextract from the llama.cpp headers. Which platform carries which library is given in brackets.

llama.cpp and ggml, release b12811 (https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp) [all platforms]
  Copyright (c) 2023-2026 The ggml authors. MIT License. Text: licenses/llama.cpp-MIT.txt.
  The libraries llama, ggml, ggml-base, the CPU backend (ggml-cpu and its x86_64 variants), the Vulkan backend (ggml-vulkan)
  [windows-x86_64, linux-x86_64] and the Metal, BLAS and RPC backends [macosx-arm64].

LLVM OpenMP runtime library, libomp.dll [windows-x86_64]
  From the llama.cpp release archive. Apache License 2.0 with LLVM Exceptions; parts under the University of Illinois/NCSA
  Open Source License and the MIT License. Text: licenses/LLVM-OpenMP-Apache-2.0-WITH-LLVM-exception.txt.

The Windows libraries use the Microsoft Visual C++ runtime of the Java runtime or the system, the Linux libraries use the GNU OpenMP
runtime (libgomp.so.1) and the Vulkan loader (libvulkan.so.1) of the system, and the macOS libraries use Accelerate and Metal of the
operating system; none of them is part of these jars.
